{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he did so, etc.; as, etc.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to say <b>toward the face of</b> etc., and it did not suffice with the statement ״וַיַּעַשׂ כֵּן״ etc. Further, it returned to say <b>as He commanded</b> etc., and this is the same statement itself that it said ״וַיַּעַשׂ כֵּן״ etc. It may intend to say this: its saying <b>וַיַּעַשׂ כֵּן</b> refers to the dismantling of the lamps and setting them down so that they would be as though new — for by this the dedication (חִנּוּךְ) is justified, as we have said. And its saying <b>אֶל מוּל פְּנֵי</b> etc. refers to the arrangement of their placement, that their openings should be toward the face of etc. And its saying <b>כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה</b> is because the command was spoken during the day, and it comes to say that then, at the time he was commanded, he performed the stated action. Therefore it says <b>כַּאֲשֶׁר</b> etc., to say that he did it at the time HaShem commanded, which is in the evening. And although we have said that there is [a possibility of] kindling during the day in the western lamp, this was only in the times of the decline of the people of HaShem, when the western lamp would go out (Yoma 39b), not in the days of Aaron, and certainly not at the beginning of the establishment of the Mishkan. Also, in its saying <b>כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה</b> etc., it alludes to make known the praise of Aaron, for what Aaron did he did not do for the sake of the distinction and the honor that HaShem had exalted him with, but rather for the sake of performing the mitzvah of HaShem, as it says (Psalms 40:9): ״לַעֲשׂוֹת רְצוֹנְךָ אֱלֹהַי חָפָצְתִּי״."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The citation (יומא לט:) is normalized to Yoma 39b; the Hebrew gives only the folio side abbreviation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:54.439949080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}